# Dashboard UI

## Philosophy

Creation workspace — calm, focused, lightweight, emotionally warm. **Not** enterprise admin aesthetics.

## Layout

- Simple navigation; clear hierarchy; lightweight controls
- **Editor:** form controls + **live preview** (side-by-side desktop; stacked/collapsible on mobile)
- Avoid overcrowded sidebars and deep nested menus

## Mobile

- Collapsible editor/preview panels
- Bottom primary actions where appropriate
- Usable on phone without desktop-only assumptions

## States

- **Loading:** skeleton loaders, smooth transitions — never blank screens
- **Empty:** friendly, guiding copy — not generic placeholders
- **Error:** clear user-facing messages

## Interactions

Immediate feedback; predictable; no delayed responses during edit.

## Performance

Lightweight during editing: minimize rerenders, avoid heavy animations, keep Zustand updates targeted.

## Wiring Routes

New dashboard features must link from UI (buttons/nav) — not only reachable by manual URL (see project-context routing).

## Priority

Clarity → responsiveness → ease of use → mobile usability → smooth editing
